cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pennylane-zksf: PennyLane device for the Zero Kelvin Simulation Foundry"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21851381
message: "If you use this device or the certification protocols it surfaces in published work, please cite the protocol paper as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ZKSF.org (Zero Kelvin Simulation Foundry)"
    email: info@zksf.org
    website: "https://zksf.org"
  - name: "Digital Venture Labs LLC"
repository-code: "https://github.com/official-dvl/pennylane-zksf"
url: "https://zksf.org"
abstract: >-
  PennyLane device exposing ZKSF simulation engines, so existing PennyLane
  circuits run against exact statevector, tensor-network, stabilizer,
  Pauli-propagation or noisy engines by naming a different device. Every
  approximate result carries a documented accuracy statement under the ZCC-v0.1
  protocol, reachable through device.error_info(). PennyLane passes a sequence
  of tapes to execute whenever it broadcasts, and those are submitted as a
  single batched request rather than one job each. Deliberately
  non-differentiable: each execution is a billed cloud job, so differentiating
  through it would issue shifted tapes and spend money invisibly.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - pennylane
  - pennylane plugin
  - quantum circuit simulation
  - tensor networks
  - error bounds
  - certification
